                <pb facs="0255" n="247" sameAs="frus:frus1937v04/pg247"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">393.11/1972: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in China</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Johnson</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Nanking</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1937-08-04T15:00:00+08:00">August 4, 1937—3
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received August 4—8:40 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>370. My 369, August 4, 2 p.m.<anchor n="39" xml:id="d240-f1"/> Following sent
                    Tientsin and repeated to Peiping and Hankow: <quote rend="blockquote">
                        <p>“August 4, 2 p.m. Your August 3, 3 p.m.<anchor n="40" xml:id="d240-f2"/>
                            and August 3, 4 p.m.,<anchor n="39" xml:id="d240-f3"/> are being
                            repeated to Hankow. Please furnish list of Americans and places of
                            residence contained in your August 3, 4 p.m., and any others in your
                            district concerning whose safety you may be in doubt to Japanese Consul
                            General for information of Japanese military and with request that
                            military take note thereof with a view to the protection of their lives
                            and property in places where Japanese may be active.”</p>
                    </quote></p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Johnson</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
